# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Without this file a build context rooted at
# the repo would bake every production secret into an image layer: .env and its
# timestamped backups, service-account JSON (for which .gitignore has no
# pattern at all), the Android keystore, and full git history.
#
# The Dockerfile's runtime stage copies only the bundled entrypoint, so this is
# the second line of defence rather than the only one - but a leaked builder
# layer is recoverable from a pushed image, so both matter.

.git
.github
.claude
.agents

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
build-output
bot/bot.cjs

android
.firebase
.vercel
graphify-out
public/pdfjs

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
*keys*.txt
map*.txt

# Rosters and student data
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.log

scripts/qaAccount.mjs
scripts/qaPassword.mjs
